WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.920
In the University's meeting rooms, the whiteboard marker caddy is the most-flagged recurring failure.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.910
A new paper asks whether naming someone responsible keeps it stocked.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:16.420
My lab piloted placards naming a caddy's Directly Responsible Individual.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:21.353
We paired sixty meeting rooms by building wing and how often they were booked.

00:00:21.653 --> 00:00:23.613
One room in each pair got the placard.

00:00:24.413 --> 00:00:27.513
Every week for twelve weeks, an auditor tested every caddy.

00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:30.063
It passed with at least three working markers,

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.003
and an eraser that wiped a test line clean.

00:00:33.903 --> 00:00:37.503
Across the term, caddies with and without a placard tracked each other.

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:40.803
Labelled ones passed fifty-seven point seven per cent of the time.

00:00:41.003 --> 00:00:42.793
Unlabelled ones, fifty-eight.

00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:47.903
The strongest predictor was the walk to the nearest stationery cupboard.

00:00:48.203 --> 00:00:52.233
Within fifteen metres of one, caddies passed seventy-four per cent of the time.

00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:55.793
Beyond fifty metres, fifty-six, placard or not.

00:00:56.793 --> 00:00:58.993
We also asked staff two questions.

00:00:59.193 --> 00:01:00.943
Could they name the person on the placard?

00:01:01.143 --> 00:01:04.623
And how confident were they that an empty caddy would be restocked?

00:01:05.423 --> 00:01:08.993
Only nine point three per cent in labelled rooms could name the person.

00:01:09.393 --> 00:01:12.273
Yet seventy-one per cent felt confident it would be restocked,

00:01:12.473 --> 00:01:15.313
against thirty-four per cent in unlabelled rooms.

00:01:16.313 --> 00:01:18.223
A placard buys reassurance.

00:01:18.523 --> 00:01:21.263
A shorter walk to the stationery cupboard buys markers.

00:01:22.163 --> 00:01:24.683
A name on a wall doesn't restock anything by itself.

00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:27.893
What it changes is how safe everyone feels not checking.
